    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0583" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1126.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My February 27, noon. Dutch steamer which arrived yesterday brought about fifteen
                    Deputies from the south, giving House a quorum. Senate still awaiting arrival of
                    at least 2 Senators for majority for presidential electoral college.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
